# Equivalent mutants: changes that test-mutation makes to the code, which no
# test can tell apart from the code, so no test can kill them. Each line lets
# one such mutant live:
#
#   <mutant> | <original> -> <replacement> | <reason>
#
# with the mutant and the change as the finding names them, and a reason that
# proves the change equivalent. Adding a line is a decision of review; prefer
# a simpler code without the mutant. A line that matches no living mutant fails
# the check. See docs/guides/mutation-tests.md.
